# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) and fill in from Supabase: Project Settings → API Keys.
# Left out, the app runs as in P1: local only, with no account UI.
# The publishable key is meant for the browser; never put a secret key (sb_secret_…) here.
# The values are built into the app, so rebuild or restart `npm run dev` after changing them.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Feature flags, built into the app like the values above (review D7). Left out, each feature stays off. Production sets
# them on Vercel; the e2e build sets them in e2e/helpers/supabase.ts (E2E_SUPABASE_ENV).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AI=1                  quick add's AI reader and Ask, through the `ai` Edge Function (needs Supabase)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AI_SETUP_CHAT=1       the setup chat too (off in Production while the AI runs on Groq's free plan)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DISCOUNT_MAP=1        the discount map beside the list on Tips → Discounts
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=     the weekly reminder's public push key (Settings → Weekly reminder; needs Supabase)

# Only for the local MCP server (mcp/, see README): the account its budget_overview and recent_entries tools sign in
# as, read-only. Use a test account: the password sits here in plain text, in this git-ignored file. Put it in double
# quotes if it holds # or spaces. The app never reads these, and without the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix they never reach the
# browser. Restart the server (in Claude Code: /mcp) after changing them.
STUDENTSBUDGET_MCP_EMAIL=
STUDENTSBUDGET_MCP_PASSWORD=
